 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "I was reading the last piece, the decorator in `scaffold.py`. This repo is a Flask-style framework called `tessel`, so the names differ from Flask's.\n\n**How the variables get there**\n- `_base_template_vars()` in `src/tessel/templating.py:21` is the built-in context processor. It returns `g`, plus `request` when a request exists.\n- Its comment says `session` is not injected here. The `session` proxy can't be replaced with a concrete object, so it comes through the normal proxy.\n- `src/tessel/sansio/scaffold.py:184` registers it by default: `template_ctx_injectors = defaultdict(list, {None: [_base_template_vars]})`.\n- `render_template`, `render_template_string`, `stream_template` and `stream_template_string` (`templating.py:136–200`) go through `_render` or `_stream`. Both call `app.fill_template_scope(ctx, context)`.\n- `App.fill_template_scope` (`src/tessel/app.py:588`) runs every injector registered under `None` (app-wide). During a request it also runs the injectors of the current bundles.\n- Each injector's returned dict is merged into the context. The values you pass to `render_template` are re-applied last, so they win on conflicts.\n\n**Adding your own variables**\n- Use the `@ctx_injector` decorator, defined as `Scaffold.ctx_injector` at `src/tessel/sansio/scaffold.py:550`. Decorate a function that returns a dict, for example `@app.ctx_injector`.\n- On an app, it runs for every template.\n- On a bundle, it only runs for templates rendered from that bundle's views.\n- To get an app-wide injector from a bundle, use `Bundle.app_ctx_injector`, which the docstring mentions. I didn't open its definition.",
